# Copy this file to .env and fill in what you need:
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# On Windows, run.bat does this for you (and generates the secrets below).
# On Linux/macOS, ./setup.sh generates the secrets below if they are missing.
#
# .env is gitignored - it's never committed, and it's never overwritten by
# `git pull` or by re-running setup.sh (setup.sh only adds/updates the
# CUDA_* lines below and fills in secrets that are missing or insecure).

# -- Ngrok (optional) ---------------------------------------------------------
# Only needed if you want other machines to join your cluster over the
# network. Leave blank for single-machine / local-only use - the ngrok
# containers will just idle without a token instead of doing anything.
# Get a free token at https://dashboard.ngrok.com/get-started/your-authtoken
NGROK_AUTHTOKEN=

# -- Security (REQUIRED) ------------------------------------------------------
# The backend refuses to start if either of these is empty, too short, or one
# of the old public defaults that used to ship in this repo.
#
# Leave them blank here: run.bat / setup.sh generate strong random values.
# To generate your own:
#   JWT_SECRET     openssl rand -base64 48     (must be base64, >= 32 bytes)
#   SERVICE_TOKEN  openssl rand -hex 24        (>= 16 characters)
#
# JWT_SECRET is the credential that lets machines in the same cluster trust each
# other's logins. To join someone else's cluster, set YOUR JWT_SECRET to THEIR
# value (ask the host over a private channel). Never post it publicly.
SERVICE_TOKEN=
JWT_SECRET=

# -- NVIDIA / CUDA (only used with docker-compose.nvidia.yml) -----------------
# Set automatically by `./setup.sh` (option 1) if you pick a non-default
# CUDA version. Leave unset to use the pinned default (CUDA 12.4 / cu122).
# CUDA_BASE_IMAGE=nvidia/cuda:12.4.1-cudnn-runtime-ubuntu22.04
# CUDA_WHEEL_TAG=cu124
